# Vercel serves the repo root statically with no build step, so anything
# listed here is reachable at a public URL unless excluded — unlike
# server.js's own isForbiddenPath() check (local dev only), Vercel has no
# equivalent guard by default.

# Database schema, RLS policies, and Edge Function source. Not secret (no
# credentials live in SQL), but a running production schema has no reason to
# be browsable at /supabase/migrations/*.sql.
supabase/

# Demo/seed runtime state — not meant to be served as a static file at all;
# the app reads it through server.js's /state.js route in dev, and production
# reads live data from Supabase instead.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash: "data/" with no anchor matches a directory
# named data/ AT ANY DEPTH (same rule as .gitignore), which silently deployed
# a build that excluded src/data/ too — the app's actual seed/catalog/history
# modules — and broke every view. This bit exactly once; keep the slash.
/data/

# The Flutter app's full source tree (large, and irrelevant to what Vercel
# serves — the built output lives in technician/, which IS deployed).
technician_app/

# Local-dev-only server; Vercel uses api/env.js + vercel.json instead (see
# api/env.js's own comment).
server.js

# Internal docs, scripts, and tooling config — no reason to be public.
docs/
scripts/
.claude/
.agents/
Dijital_Pest_Control_Platformu_Teknik_Dokum.md
Repellent Online sistem yol haritası.docx
README.md

# Belt-and-suspenders: .env is already git-ignored (never reaches the repo
# Vercel builds from), but excluded here too in case that ever changes.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
